# Code owners — review that a CI gate cannot substitute for.
#
# Flyway migrations are listed because artifact rollback (ADR-028/029) depends
# on every migration being expand-only, and `scripts/check-migration-safety.sh`
# can only catch the unambiguous breaks. The judgement calls it cannot make —
# a constraint tightened rather than widened, a backfill that assumes the new
# code is already deployed, a change that is technically additive but
# semantically incompatible — are exactly what a human review is for.
/backend/persistence/src/main/resources/db/migration/ @yannisyoussef

# The deployment contract with the Infinity Ops platform: what GitHub sends,
# what it is allowed to hold, and what a green run is permitted to claim
# (ADR-030). A change here can quietly reintroduce a host credential or turn a
# handoff back into a false deployment success.
/.github/workflows/                                   @yannisyoussef
/scripts/gitlab-handoff.sh                            @yannisyoussef
/scripts/check-migration-safety.sh                    @yannisyoussef
/scripts/validate-image-digest.sh                     @yannisyoussef
/deploy/                                              @yannisyoussef

# Accepted ADRs are authoritative (CLAUDE.md); they are amended by new ADRs,
# not edited in passing.
/docs/adr/                                            @yannisyoussef

# The credential path (ADR-032). A change here can weaken authentication in
# ways no gate can see: the format's entropy claim, the constant-time
# comparison, the bootstrap window that closes itself, or the single response
# allowed to carry a plaintext credential. The tests assert today's behaviour;
# only a human can judge whether a change to that behaviour is intended.
/backend/domain/src/main/kotlin/email/testinbox/domain/tenant/     @yannisyoussef
/backend/application/src/main/kotlin/email/testinbox/application/usecase/AuthenticateApiKey.kt @yannisyoussef
/backend/application/src/main/kotlin/email/testinbox/application/usecase/ApiKeyLifecycle.kt    @yannisyoussef
/backend/api/src/main/kotlin/email/testinbox/api/auth/             @yannisyoussef

# The hand-authored REST contract is the source of truth (ADR-022); the
# compatibility gate catches breaking shapes, not breaking meanings.
/backend/api/contract/openapi.yaml                                 @yannisyoussef
